    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW25PFxuq2GjykReQ26LTWPmi)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Order: 2 of 2, merge after #457.\n- Depends on: #457 (`sp-echo-help-set`, `sp-echo-help-format` in `sp-interaction`). This PR is stacked on its branch `457-echo-area-help-hints`, so the diff shows only this PR's changes.\n- If merged first (into #457's branch): fine. If its base were `main` before #457: load error, `sp-echo-help-set` undefined in the report buffers.\n- Conflicts with: nothing else open (#455, #456 do not touch these modules); `sp-litnotes-meta.el` may touch near #455/#443 but not the same hunks.\n- After merging #457: GitHub retargets this PR to `main`; if it does not, change the base to `main` by hand. Do not rename or delete `457-echo-area-help-hints` before that.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Request:** the linting and batch-processing interfaces (and every other buffer that lists its keys) show them as echo-area hints like `nano-help.el`, reusing the helper of #457, so all help keys look the same.\n- **Converted** (all use `sp-echo-help-set`, list of `(KEY DESCRIPTION [STRONG])`):\n  - `sp-batch-report-mode`: shared by every batch command (litnote titles/refs/meta, author notes, tag lint, normalise, BibTeX lint, property conversion). The hints follow what the report can do (`d`/`u`, `A`, `g` only when it has the function); `A Apply` and `q Quit` are bold. `sp-batch-report-open` sets them again once the functions are set.\n  - Footnote lint: the header line keeps only the progress; the keys follow the phase of the run (`sp-org-lint-fn--render` sets them). The obsolete old view gets them too.\n  - Litnote status table: counts stay in the header line; the keys are hints.\n  - Author notes report (old view): the key line at the bottom is gone.\n  - Author works from BibTeX report: the key line under the title is gone.\n  - Tag lint report (old view): the key line at the bottom is gone.\n  - Backlink check (`sp-vulpea-backlink-check`): the key line under the title is gone.\n  - Relationship graph view (`sp-graphs`): the title line keeps the depth; the keys are hints.\n- Docs are bullet lists (`sp-batch-report.org`, `sp-org-lint.org`, `sp-org-tag-lint.org`, `sp-litnotes-meta.org`, `sp-vulpea.org`, `sp-graphs.org`); `.el` files re-tangled from them. `when-let*` only; no CHANGELOG edit.\n- **Tested** (Emacs 29.3 batch): 18 `sp-batch-report` tests pass (1 new), `sp-echo-help` 4 and `sp-fetch-inbox` 15 still pass; syntax check of all touched modules.\n- **Untested by Claude:** everything outside the batch report (footnote lint, litnote status table, author notes, tag lint, backlink check, graph view): their tests or modules need your real vulpea/`sp-globals` environment. Also the look in the real GUI with your theme, and how the grid fits a narrow frame (the batch report has up to 8 hints).\n\n## Manual testing\n\nNeeds #457 checked out first (this branch includes it).\n\n- [ ] `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 459-echo-help-linting-uis; git checkout 459-echo-help-linting-uis`, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n- [ ] `cd ~/.config/emacs-modular; emacs -Q --batch -L libraries/modules/funct -L libraries/modules/base -L libraries/modules/academic -L libraries/modules/ui -L libraries/modules/vulpea -l tests/sp-batch-report-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit` → 18 pass (more `-L` if Emacs asks)\n- [ ] `M-x sp-litnotes-titles-dryrun`: no keys in the header line; the echo area shows the grid of hints with `Apply` and `Quit` bold (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] In that report press `d` on an entry: the \"dropped\" message is not overwritten; the hints return after the next command\n- [ ] A report with no apply function (for example a preview-only one): no `Apply` hint\n- [ ] `M-x sp-org-lint-footnotes-dryrun`: while scanning the header shows progress and the echo area only `[q] Quit`; when done the full hints appear (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] After `a` apply in the footnote lint: header says \"applied\", hints change to `Visit / Rescan / Quit`\n- [ ] `M-x sp-litnotes-meta-status-report`: counts in the header, hints in the echo area (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] `M-x sp-author-notes-bibtex` (or its report command): no key line in the buffer, hints in the echo area (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] `M-x sp-org-tag-lint` with `sp-batch-report-interface` set to `old`: no footer line, hints show `Register tag at point` (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] The backlink check of a note (`sp-vulpea-backlink-check`): title only, hints `Visit / Move / Refresh / Quit` (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] The relationship graph view: title with depth, hints `Expand / Visit / Re-scope / Rebuild`; `TAB`, `c`, `g` still work (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] Narrow the frame: the hints wrap or shrink, nothing runs off the window\n- [ ] Switch to another buffer: no stray hints there; `*Messages*` has no hint lines\n- [ ] Regression: `RET`, `n`, `p`, `d`, `u`, `A`, `g`, `q` still work in a report\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard any local edits made while testing: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .` (and `git clean -fd` only after checking `git clean -nd`).\n- Return to the previous branch of the stack (`457-echo-area-help-hints`) if you only test part of it, otherwise to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`.\n- Optionally delete the test branch locally: `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D 459-echo-help-linting-uis`; the remote copy stays until the PR is merged or closed.\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`) so the config matches main again.\n- The dry runs only read the vault; no vault restore is needed.\n- Fish shell works for all of the above; no yadm steps.\n\n</details>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiA3876SADjpTLYKDZ5)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiA3876SADjpTLYKDZ5\n",
